Hmm, to follow through a bit on this, I wrongly blamed Sweave for
formatting, and underestimated the amount of work required to make pdf
versions of the manual 'pretty'. Sweave does not play a role in creating
the manual. Instead, the R tools for processing the vignette place the
usage section in a 'verbatim' tex environment (similarly for the
examples code, too, I think). Thus the 'fix' is for each package
maintainer to write 'man' pages that are consistent with reasonable
display of this formatting -- a fairly daunting task.

For the record, the way man pages are generated as pdf is

  R CMD Rd2dvi --pdf <pkg_name-or-Rd_file>

