From smyth at wehi.EDU.AU  Mon Jun 15 03:41:30 2009
From: smyth at wehi.EDU.AU (Gordon K Smyth)
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2009 11:41:30 +1000 (AUS Eastern Standard Time)
Subject: [BioC] Fixes to limma treat() function
Message-ID: <Pine.WNT.4.64.0906151134560.4208@PC602.alpha.wehi.edu.au>

I've committed a major bug fix to the treat() function of the limma 
package.  Users of this function should re-install limma 2.18.2 or 2.19.2 
from Bioconductor.

I've introduced a new function topTreat().  Here's an example calling 
sequence:

   fit <- lmFit(y, design)
   fit <- treat(fit, lfc=0.1)
   topTreat(fit, coef=2)

Best wishes
Gordon


