Hi John,

I might be missing what you mean ...

To read microarray data in a generic format, you have to tell limma the 
column names of the data columns you want it to read.  This means that you 
have to check first yourself, eg using Excel or a text editor, to see what 
column headings the files contain.

Given a generic format file, limma simply finds the first line in the file 
which contains the required column names, skipping any earlier lines, and 
reads from there.

Best wishes
Gordon

