From P.D.Moerland at amc.uva.nl  Mon Jun 29 22:06:43 2009
From: P.D.Moerland at amc.uva.nl (P.D. Moerland)
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2009 22:06:43 +0200
Subject: [BioC] Annotation.db: how automatically call a mapping?
In-Reply-To: <5FC630F6B49E654293B1F532B618BC6E012FCD99@scomp0039.wurnet.nl>
References: <5FC630F6B49E654293B1F532B618BC6E012FCD99@scomp0039.wurnet.nl>
Message-ID: <8b17924b56048332.4a493af3@amc.uva.nl>

Dear Guido,

A few weeks back I was struggling with the same problem and came up with this solution:


makeMapping <- function(annotPkg,str="SYMBOL",ids){
	do.call(library,list(annotPkg))
	annotPkg = sub(".db","",annotPkg)
	f = function(x) mget(ids,x,ifnotfound=NA)
	annot = do.call(f,list(get(paste(annotPkg,str,sep=""))))
       return(annot)
}

Just as an example:

> makeMapping("moe430a.db",str="SYMBOL",ids=c("1415670_at","1415671_at"))

$`1415670_at`
[1] "Copg"

$`1415671_at`
[1] "Atp6v0d1"


best,
Perry

